13267	{"artifactId":"LLD-315d510cb28100e2-s7","entry":{"id":"review-949be370128da0837192124c404c791e","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:21:34.333Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac29–ac34 (submit approved artifacts as one request linked from the stage issue, refuse missing prerequisites, block the next stage until completion, sign off all artifacts together, no change for stages the policy does not list) are each designed in openSignoff and signoffCompletionHook, and revising an open request is left to s8.","evidence":"DEF.md:224-229 states ac29–ac34. §2.1 and §2.2 design each one: openSignoff's prerequisite checks and single request, the hook's awaiting-signoff/continue/signed-off branches, and the 'continue' answer for an unlisted stage. Revision is excluded and assigned to s8. [files: docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/DEF.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"ac35 (when a signed-off artifact's records are shown, review and approval look as before and signoff is shown separately) is designed down to a surface that shows it.","evidence":"§2.5 and §3.4 add only a derived SignoffView. Its call sites are approval-view.ts and delivery/load.ts, which hold status lists (APPROVED_OR_BEYOND at approval-view.ts:18 and APPROVED_STATUSES at load.ts:54), not renderers. No renderer in the terminal, review output or artifact markdown is named that calls signoffViewOf, so nothing in the design actually shows signoff separately. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/approval-view.ts, src/workflow/delivery/load.ts]","action":"Name the display surfaces (for example the terminal's artifact/approval view and the artifact markdown) that render SignoffView, and add a test that checks the rendered output.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The lifecycle already models signoff: a Signoff type with revision, request Reference and state; the open-signoff, signoff-changes and signed-off operations; and the in-signoff, changes-requested and signed-off statuses. open-signoff needs a request Reference.","evidence":"types.ts:131-137 defines Signoff { revision, request: Reference, state, actors, at }. lifecycle.ts:43-45 defines open-signoff approved→in-signoff, signoff-changes in-signoff→changes-requested and signed-off in-signoff→signed-off. lifecycle.ts:250-260 requires detail.request through needReference and moves the latest open Signoff. reconcileLifecycle (lifecycle.ts:163-168) sends the artifact back to draft on a content change and keeps signoffs at their revisions. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"SignoffRequestSpec and SignoffRequestRef are placeholders in the port, and the GitHub adapter's signoff methods are unsupported today.","evidence":"port.ts:45-54 has 'Minimal placeholder; s7 extends it by amendment' with only { title, body } and { ref }. github-adapter.ts:13 says 'GitHub declares {claim, issue-create}. The signoff methods return rejected'. github-adapter.ts:203-204 has openSignoffRequest: () => unsupported(...). [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Registering the hook once at daemon start, beside registerParkOfferProvider, makes it run on every gate call that should be blocked on signoff.","evidence":"registeredHook is a per-process module variable (gate.ts:96-100). The terminal runs the gate in its own process: cli/services/index.ts:101-102 says 'The terminal runs the team gate in its own process' and registers registerParkOfferProvider there as well as in daemon/steps/workflow-step/park-offer.ts:30. If the hook is registered only at daemon start, gate calls from the terminal process (release, and any author/build/open-signoff run there) never consult it. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts, src/cli/services/index.ts, src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/park-offer.ts]","action":"Also register signoffCompletionHook in makeServices (the terminal process), or state that no hooked action runs outside the daemon and test that.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The completion hook, as reused from sc4, can apply 'signed-off' / 'signoff-changes' through LifecycleService and read the heads before returning its GateOutcome, so recording is all-or-none and a partial failure comes back as refused.","evidence":"CompletionHook is synchronous: gate.ts:94 has `(repo, unit, port) => GateOutcome | 'continue'`, and consultHook calls `registeredHook(repo, unit, port)` with no await (gate.ts:123). teamGate is synchronous too. LifecycleService.apply is `async apply(...): Promise<ApplyResult>` (lifecycle-service.ts:78) and has no synchronous form. The hook therefore cannot await the lifecycle writes or head reads that §2.2 and §5 rely on ('reports a partial failure as refused', 'does not release the claim'). It would either return before anything is recorded or need sc4's hook type changed, which s5 owns. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts]","action":"Either propose an sc4 amendment that makes CompletionHook/teamGate async and lists every teamGate caller, or redesign so the hook only reads synchronously and the signed-off recording happens in an async step before the gate is consulted. State the choice and its error handling.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"SignoffRecord, SignoffView, openSignoff, signoffRecordsOf and SignoffRefusedError are new and do not duplicate existing code.","evidence":"A grep for Signoff across src/workflow finds only the lifecycle Signoff type and operations, the port placeholders, the policy's signoffStages and the gate's 'awaiting-signoff' outcome. There is no SignoffRecord, signoffRecordsOf, signoffView or team/signoff.ts. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts, src/workflow/tracker/port.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"openSignoff can go through the gate's 'open-signoff' action, and a repeat call after a partial recording 'finds the open request for them and records the rest instead of opening a second one' (§5).","evidence":"'open-signoff' is in HOOKED (gate.ts:117), so teamGate consults the registered hook before reading the holder (gate.ts:267-268). The hook receives no action argument (gate.ts:94), so it cannot tell open-signoff from author. Per §2.2 it returns { kind: 'awaiting-signoff' } whenever the unit has an open request. After a partial recording, the heads already moved hold an open Signoff, so the repeat openSignoff is refused with TeamGateRefusedError and never reaches the 'record the rest' path. The same applies to opening a second stage's request on the same unit (for example the HLD while the Define is in signoff, both on the epic unit), which the design does not discuss. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"Pass the action to the hook (an sc4 amendment), or have openSignoff skip the hook's awaiting-signoff for the artifacts it is submitting. State the rule for a second stage of the same unit, and test the partial-retry path through the real gate.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"On completion the hook can release the claim through the gate's release action whoever triggers the next stage ('when someone starts the next stage, then it proceeds', ac32).","evidence":"release() (gate.ts:314-337) skips the hook (insideHook), but for a non-administrator it reads the holder and refuses unless the actor is the holder: 'only the holder (...) or a policy administrator may release this stage'. The hook gets only (repo, unit, port), not the issue or actor. When the next stage is started by someone other than the holder, release refuses, and the design does not say whether the hook then refuses, continues, or records signed-off without releasing. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"State who releases on completion and what happens when release is refused (for example clear the assignee directly through port.setAssignee on the unit issue, with an sc4 amendment if needed), and add a test where a non-holder triggers completion.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No new stored field is needed: older records carry Lifecycle.signoffs (possibly empty), a content change leaves signoffs at their old revision, and pre-policy approvals are grandfathered from the policy anchor without being written.","evidence":"Lifecycle.signoffs is a required array (types.ts:150), backfilled by convert (convert/backfill.ts references signoff). reconcileLifecycle keeps signoffs on a content change (lifecycle.ts:152,168). TeamPolicy.source has firstCommitTime and anchorKnown (team/types.ts:47-48), filled by policy-parser.ts:73-74, so a grandfathered record can be computed with nothing written. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, src/workflow/team/types.ts, src/workflow/team/policy-parser.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design stays inside s7: it registers rather than redesigns the sc4 hook, extends sc1's signoff types only by amendment, and leaves revision of an open request to s8.","evidence":"§4 consumes sc4 (registers the hook, returns GateOutcome) and proposes the sc1 SignoffRequestSpec/Ref change by amendment, which matches port.ts:45-54 ('s7 extends it by amendment'). gate.ts:90 says 'declared here, registered by s7'. Revision is deferred to s8. The fixes needed for the HIGH findings above (an async hook, an action argument) would touch sc4, so they must go through an amendment and not an in-place edit. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts, src/workflow/tracker/port.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every failure has a detection and a stated response: prerequisite failures, gate refusal, tracker open failure, partial recording at open and at completion, unreachable state read, changes requested, and content changed after signoff.","evidence":"§5 lists eight error cases, each with detection, response and user impact. They match real signals: PortResult failure kinds (port.ts:22-26), IllegalTransitionError from nextLifecycle (lifecycle.ts:216-217,258) and the gate's refused/no-issue outcomes (gate.ts:32-37). Whether some of these responses can be carried out at all is reported under new-versus-reuse and change-sites (the synchronous hook, the hooked open-signoff). [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of ac29–ac35 maps to at least one named test, on fixtures and seams that exist.","evidence":"§6's acceptance table maps ac29–ac35 to signoff.test.ts, signoff-hook.test.ts, signoff-view.test.ts, github-signoff.test.ts, signoff-e2e.test.ts and a smoke test. The fixtures named exist: src/workflow/__tests__/lifecycle-fixtures.ts and _setGateDepsForTests (gate.ts:87). The ac35 test checks the view function only, not a rendered surface (see coverage-of-intent). [files: src/workflow/__tests__/lifecycle-fixtures.ts, src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":2,"med":3,"low":8,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-22T13:21:34.333Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
433	{"artifactId":"LLD-315d510cb28100e2-s7","entry":{"id":"f6af61b8b7254d2d8da57a2162a2c932","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:23:18.459Z","operation":"review","revision":{"number":1,"contentHash":"ef674e5fe26b2f6d87accb335469e48ee61659b94970b473550ca74c01005cd6"},"outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"reviewed by the daemon: block","data":{"counts":{"high":2,"med":3,"low":8}}}}}
13650	{"artifactId":"LLD-315d510cb28100e2-s7","entry":{"id":"review-57db127993ee10044acd9f4c72ad26fd","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-22T14:56:37.665Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every upstream acceptance criterion for s7 (ac29–ac35 in the DEF) is designed: submission with linking, refusal naming a missing prerequisite, refusal while awaiting signoff, settling at the next-stage attempt, all-together signoff, unlisted stages unaffected, and signoff shown apart from review.","evidence":"DEF.md:224-230 lists ac29..ac35 with exactly these behaviours. The LLD covers each one: openSignoff/openSignoffRequest for ac29, the prerequisite refusal for ac30, the awaiting-signoff hook outcome for ac31 (describeOutcome in gate.ts:65 prints the request ref), settleSignoff for ac32/ac33, 'continue' for unlisted stages for ac34, and signoffViewOf for ac35. None of s8's revision flow is built here. [files: docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/DEF.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"CompletionHook is synchronous and receives no action. consultHook calls it only for author, build, open-signoff, revise and release, and it is declared but not registered anywhere.","evidence":"gate.ts:94 `export type CompletionHook = (repo: string, unit: UnitRef, port: TrackerPort) => GateOutcome | 'continue'`; gate.ts:117 HOOKED = ['author','build','open-signoff','revise','release']; gate.ts:123 `return registeredHook(repo, unit, port)`. The only reference to registerCompletionHook is its definition at gate.ts:100. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The GitHub adapter's openSignoffRequest and readSignoffState are unsupported today.","evidence":"github-adapter.ts:203-204 `openSignoffRequest: () => unsupported('signoff requests'), readSignoffState: () => unsupported('reading signoff state')`. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Editing an artifact after signoff returns its head to draft and keeps the older signoff at its revision.","evidence":"lifecycle.ts:164-168: when the content changed, reconcileLifecycle returns `{ ...next.lifecycle, status: 'draft', revision: {...} }`. The comment at lines 150-153 says approval, review and signoffs stay at the revision numbers they were made at. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Lifecycle.signoffs and the open-signoff, signoff-changes and signed-off operations already exist and are reused. They are not redefined.","evidence":"types.ts:131-137 defines Signoff { revision, request: Reference, state, actors, at }, and types.ts:150 has `signoffs: readonly Signoff[]`. lifecycle.ts:43-45 has 'open-signoff' from approved to in-signoff, and 'signoff-changes' and 'signed-off' from in-signoff. lifecycle.ts:250-260 appends a signoff or moves the latest open one. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"TeamPolicy exposes signoffStages and source.anchorKnown, which the design reads for stage listing and grandfathering.","evidence":"team/types.ts:22 `signoffStages: readonly SignoffStage[]` (DEF|HLD|LLD|BUILD), and types.ts:43-49 `source { ... firstCommitTime, anchorKnown }`. [files: src/workflow/team/types.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Given (repo, unit, port, action), the hook can tell which stage an author or build action follows ('author and build map to the stage they follow').","evidence":"author-gate.ts:28-31 maps BOTH design.story and plan runs to the same story unit `{ unit: 'story', ... }`, and teamGate is called as `teamGate(intent.repoPath, unit, 'author', intent.workflow)`. The `authoring` workflow goes only to teamGate (gate.ts:254) and never reaches consultHook (gate.ts:120-123), and the planned signature adds only `action`. On a story unit, the hook therefore cannot tell authoring the LLD (which follows the HLD, on the epic unit) from authoring the plan (which follows the LLD, on the same unit). Built as written, the hook either blocks LLD authoring on the LLD's own open signoff, or fails to check the HLD's signoff. [files: src/workflow/team/author-gate.ts, src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"Pass the authoring workflow (or the followed stage) to the hook as well as the action. Define the mapping from (unit, action, authoring) to the followed stage's unit and artifact, including design.story on a story unit following the HLD on the epic unit, and test each case.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The listed change sites cover making the GitHub adapter usable for signoff: implementing the two methods at github-adapter.ts:203-218.","evidence":"github-adapter.ts:54 `const CAPABILITIES = new Set<Capability>(['claim', 'issue-create'])`. loadTracker (github-adapter.ts:215-217) rejects any `needed` capability that is not declared. port.ts:20 defines 'signoff-request' and 'completion' capabilities. The design never says to declare them or which capability set openSignoff and settleSignoff load the tracker with. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts, src/workflow/tracker/port.ts]","action":"State that the GitHub adapter declares 'signoff-request' (and 'completion' if it is used), and that openSignoff and settleSignoff load the port with those capabilities. Add this to the change sites and the contract test.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"DeliveryItemDescription can 'gain a signoff entry separate from review and approval' at describe.ts:59 and load.ts:54.","evidence":"The type is defined at delivery/types.ts:304-308, which the design does not list. It is a per-kind discriminated union: epic {problem, summary}, story {purpose, size}, issue {...}, task {}. It carries no review or approval fields, so 'separate from review and approval' does not fit this type, and a signoff field would have to be added per variant. [files: src/workflow/delivery/types.ts, src/workflow/delivery/describe.ts]","action":"Name the actual delivery type that shows each artifact's review and approval (or add the field to each variant explicitly), and list delivery/types.ts as a change site.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Older records without signoffs keep working: a missing lifecycle decodes with an empty signoffs list.","evidence":"decode.ts:39 defaults to `signoffs: []`. storage.ts:192 and backfill.ts:178 (`signoffs: existing?.signoffs ?? []`) do the same, and convert/apply.ts:76 writes `signoffs: []`. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/decode.ts, src/workflow/convert/backfill.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Every artifact is recorded open-signoff with 'the same request Reference', taken from the port's SignoffRequestRef.","evidence":"Signoff.request is a `Reference` (types.ts:133), and nextLifecycle's needReference (lifecycle.ts:197-200) requires a non-empty entityId, type and relation. The port returns `SignoffRequestRef { ref: string }`, plus an optional url per AMD-16. The design never defines how the ref becomes a Reference, which entityId, type and relation are stored, or how signoffRecordsOf and settle turn the stored Reference back into a SignoffRequestRef to group and read requests. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, src/workflow/tracker/port.ts]","action":"Specify the conversion between SignoffRequestRef and Reference (the field values and the inverse) used by openSignoff, settleSignoff and signoffRecordsOf.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The trailing action argument on CompletionHook (owned by s5/sc4) comes through a filed sc4 amendment.","evidence":"The only pending s7 amendment is AMD-315d510cb28100e2-16, of type sharedContract.fieldAdd on contractId 'sc1' (SignoffRequestSpec). The other AMD files that mention the completion hook (AMD-13/14/15) concern registerParkOfferProvider, and 14 and 15 are rejected. No amendment changes the CompletionHook signature, yet the LLD section 3.3 says '(sc4 amendment)'. [files: .insrc/artifacts/AMD-315d510cb28100e2-16.json, src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"File a sharedContract amendment on sc4 for the CompletionHook action argument (plus the authoring or followed-stage input), or drop the change.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"A submitter who does not hold the claim is detected because teamGate with action open-signoff returns held-by-other or refused.","evidence":"gate.ts:276 `if (holder === null && !CLAIMING.has(action)) return allowed();`, and CLAIMING is only author and build (gate.ts:135). On an unassigned stage, teamGate(…, 'open-signoff') returns allowed for anyone, so a non-holder can open a signoff request. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"Require openSignoff to see a holder equal to the actor (treat an unassigned stage as a refusal), or state that an unassigned stage may be submitted by anyone, and test that case.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The prerequisite check (approvalStateOf plus lifecycleReviewOf, i.e. other-party review in the lifecycle) works for every stage listed in signoffStages, including BUILD.","evidence":"lifecycle.ts:192 REVIEW_REQUIRED_KINDS = ['DEF','HLD','LLD']. gates.ts:730-733 says BUILD's review is the 'code' review. code-review/gate.ts:9-15 reads the CodeReviewArtifact (CR record) 'NEVER on the lifecycle review'. A BUILD head has no lifecycle.review, so lifecycleReviewOf always fails for BUILD, while the starter policy lists BUILD (starter-policy.ts:24). Built as written, every BUILD submission is refused for a missing review. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts, src/workflow/code-review/gate.ts, src/workflow/team/starter-policy.ts]","action":"For BUILD, check the Story's code-review record (CR, other party, verdict not block) instead of lifecycle.review, and add a BUILD case to signoff.test.ts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.3","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A failure inside the hook is detectable and keeps the stage blocked, not let through.","evidence":"gate.ts:124: consultHook catches any throw from the hook and returns `refused('the completion hook failed: …')`, and teamGate returns that refusal (gate.ts:267-268). [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion ac29–ac35 maps to at least one named test, and the registration in both processes is tested.","evidence":"The acceptance-mapping table gives tests for ac29..ac35 that match the DEF criteria (DEF.md:224-230). signoff-registration.test.ts covers the daemon start and makeServices. makeServices exists at src/cli/services/index.ts:100 and already registers a gate provider there (line 102), so the test target is real. The real GitHub flow is a reported smoke test, not run by the gate. [files: src/cli/services/index.ts, docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/DEF.md]","action":"Add tests for the HIGH findings: the hook's followed-stage mapping for design.story versus plan on a story unit, and the BUILD prerequisite check.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":2,"med":5,"low":9,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-22T14:56:37.665Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
