11389	{"artifactId":"LLD-315d510cb28100e2-s7","entry":{"id":"review-24647342101fea2120df23b560749de5","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-22T15:18:34.688Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac29–ac35 (DEF.md:224-230) are each designed: submission with prerequisites (ac29/ac30), blocking the next stage while open (ac31), settle-at-next-stage with all-together recording (ac32/ac33), unlisted stages unaffected (ac34), signoff shown apart from review and approval (ac35).","evidence":"DEF.md:224-230 lists ac29..ac35 with the same wording the LLD addresses in §2 (openSignoff, settleSignoff, signoffCompletionHook) and §3.5-3.7 (display surfaces). Revision flows are left to s8, as the adjacent scope says. [files: docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/DEF.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"BUILD is a submittable signoff stage (SignoffStage includes BUILD) and the design lets an approved, code-reviewed BUILD be opened for signoff.","evidence":"Approving a BUILD calls completeIfRolledUp on the STORY (gates.ts:945-949). When the roll-up holds, that completes the Story and cascades 'complete' onto its members LLD, PLAN and BUILD (lifecycle.ts:349-362 unitMembers; lifecycle-service.ts:110-115, 248-258). The members end up in 'completed'. LIFECYCLE_TABLE allows 'open-signoff' only from ['approved'] (lifecycle.ts:43), and 'complete' has from ['approved','signed-off'], so the intended order is approve → signoff → complete. The LLD never holds Story completion (or the BUILD cascade) until signoff when BUILD (or LLD) is in signoffStages. So openSignoff on a BUILD — or on an LLD submitted after the Story completed — throws IllegalTransitionError ('open-signoff is not a step from completed'), and ac29 cannot be met for BUILD. [files: src/workflow/gates.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts]","action":"Design how Story completion waits for signoff when the policy lists BUILD (or LLD): for example, completeIfRolledUp or rollUp skips/defers completion while a listed stage is not signed off, and settle runs the completion after signed-off. Then add the change site (gates.ts completeThroughService / lifecycle-service rollUp) and a test.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"CompletionHook is synchronous, receives (repo, unit, port) only and no action; consultHook calls it only for author, build, open-signoff, revise and release, and is shipped unregistered.","evidence":"gate.ts:94 `export type CompletionHook = (repo: string, unit: UnitRef, port: TrackerPort) => GateOutcome | 'continue';` gate.ts:117 HOOKED set; gate.ts:120-126 consultHook; registerCompletionHook is called only in tests (grep). [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"teamGate returns allowed for open-signoff on an unassigned stage, so openSignoff must check the holder itself.","evidence":"gate.ts:135 CLAIMING = author, build; gate.ts:276 `if (holder === null && !CLAIMING.has(action)) return allowed();` [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The GitHub adapter declares only claim and issue-create, and openSignoffRequest/readSignoffState are unsupported stubs.","evidence":"github-adapter.ts:54 `new Set<Capability>(['claim', 'issue-create'])`; :203-204 `openSignoffRequest: () => unsupported('signoff requests')`, `readSignoffState: () => unsupported(...)`. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Lifecycle.signoffs and the open-signoff / signoff-changes / signed-off operations already exist with a Reference request, so SignoffRecord can be derived and need not be stored.","evidence":"types.ts:131-137 Signoff { revision, request: Reference, state, actors, at }; Lifecycle.signoffs at :150. lifecycle.ts:250-261: open-signoff appends {state:'open'}, and needReference requires entityId/type/relation (:197-200). signoff-changes/signed-off move the latest open signoff. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"approvalStateOf and lifecycleReviewOf exist as sync meta readers for checking prerequisites.","evidence":"approval-view.ts:30 approvalStateOf(meta) and :45 lifecycleReviewOf(meta). approvalStateOf counts in-signoff/changes-requested/signed-off/completed as 'approved' (APPROVED_OR_BEYOND :18), so the design's extra comparison of approval.revision with the head revision is needed and is stated. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/approval-view.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"settleSignoff is 'awaited at the async entry points that attempt a next stage, in the daemon and in the terminal'; that inventory is complete enough to build.","evidence":"The LLD names no concrete call sites for settle. The guarded next-stage entries are many: assertMayAuthor in daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/start.ts:61, plan.ts:40, step.ts:38, synthesize.ts:40,70; daemon/workflow-rpc.ts:183,342,483; team/handoff.ts:688; assertMayBuild in build-step/phases/implement.ts:68,144 and validate.ts:222,330,424; plus the terminal path. Without settle at an entry, a completed request stays unsettled, and the hook refuses that entry ('unsettled-completed refusal') forever. [files: src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/start.ts, src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts, src/daemon/steps/build-step/phases/implement.ts, src/daemon/steps/build-step/phases/validate.ts]","action":"List the settle call sites (at least the start phase of workflow_step, workflow-rpc, and build implement), say which entry points skip settle and rely on the hook alone, and test that each listed one awaits settle.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The terminal runs the gate in its own process, so the hook must be registered both in the daemon and in makeServices.","evidence":"cli/services/index.ts:29,102 registers registerParkOfferProvider in the terminal; the daemon registers it in daemon/steps/workflow-step/park-offer.ts:30. The same two places fit registerSignoffHook. [files: src/cli/services/index.ts, src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/park-offer.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Adding trailing optional action/authoring arguments to CompletionHook keeps existing 3-argument hooks working, and SignoffRequestSpec/Ref are placeholders to be extended by amendment.","evidence":"gate.ts:94 hook type; the existing test hooks (gate.test.ts:218-366) take ≤3 args, so extra args are harmless in TS. port.ts:45-54 'Minimal placeholder; s7 extends it by amendment.' The untracked AMD-315d510cb28100e2-16 is present. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts, src/workflow/tracker/port.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design changes the sc4 CompletionHook signature (owned by s5) and the sc1 request types (owned by s1) only through amendments, and leaves revision to s8.","evidence":"§3.2 cites the pending sc1 amendment AMD-315d510cb28100e2-16; §3.4 states it is an sc4 amendment; the untracked AMD-…-17 is present. Revision of an open request is left to s8 (§5 'revises through s8's flow'). [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts, src/workflow/tracker/port.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The hook keeps the next stage blocked whenever a followed stage has an open or unsettled request.","evidence":"In teamGate (gate.ts:257-264), when teamContext fails with no-issue (issue creation failed) and the action is author with no artifact yet, the gate returns allowFirstAuthor before consultHook runs (gate.ts:267). assertMayAuthor then lets it through (author-gate.ts:42). So a first design.story turn on a story whose issue cannot be created starts while the epic's HLD request is open. Neither the error cases nor the edge-case table cover this. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts, src/workflow/team/author-gate.ts]","action":"State the first-author/no-issue case. Either consult the signoff hook before the allowFirstAuthor exception (the hook judges a different unit) or accept the gap explicitly, and add a test.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Idempotent settle across two clones: signed-off on an already-completed signoff is detectable and skipped.","evidence":"lifecycle.ts:257-258 signed-off/signoff-changes throw unless the latest signoff is open, and status must be in-signoff (:44-45). Settle can read the latest signoff state first and skip, as the edge case says. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion ac29–ac35 maps to at least one named test.","evidence":"The §6 acceptance mapping lists proving tests for ac29..ac35 in signoff.test.ts, signoff-hook.test.ts, github-signoff.test.ts, signoff-view.test.ts and signoff-e2e.test.ts. Fixtures use the existing _setGateDepsForTests seam (gate.ts:87). No test covers BUILD signoff after Story completion (see coverage-of-intent). [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"Add a test that opens signoff on a BUILD whose Story roll-up would otherwise complete it.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":2,"low":11,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-22T15:18:34.688Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
434	{"artifactId":"LLD-315d510cb28100e2-s7","entry":{"id":"c3194e25cec7416e94fff42b923218e6","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-22T15:20:38.475Z","operation":"review","revision":{"number":3,"contentHash":"3516dc35f79467e10d9714a7ad772596c4b0bed70e1eae7626b112defb46ffe5"},"outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"reviewed by the daemon: block","data":{"counts":{"high":1,"med":2,"low":11}}}}}
12733	{"artifactId":"LLD-315d510cb28100e2-s7","entry":{"id":"review-d954a98d84f08373c8c82a83fb5c6854","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-22T15:28:34.467Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac29–ac35 (DEF.md:224-230) are each designed: submission of chosen artifacts linked from the stage issue, prerequisite refusal, next-stage refusal while open, settle-at-next-stage, all-together recording, unlisted stage unaffected, signoff shown apart from review/approval.","evidence":"DEF.md:224-230 states ac29-ac35; the LLD gives openSignoff (ac29/ac30), blockedBySignoff/settleForAttempt (ac31/ac32/ac33), the no-policy/unlisted paths (ac34) and signoffViewOf on ArtifactGate/DeliveryEvidenceEntry/chain (ac35). No non-goal (s8 revision flow, s6 park, s1 adapter extraction) is built here. [files: docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/DEF.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"When the policy lists BUILD, its signoff request is eventually settled and the held Story completes.","evidence":"followedStageOf returns null for 'anything that follows BUILD', and settleForAttempt makes no tracker call except for the followed stage. So nothing ever reads a BUILD request's state. signoffHoldsCompletion keeps the Story approved-not-completed until the BUILD is signed off, which is never recorded. rollUp/completeIfRolledUp (lifecycle.ts:332-347, lifecycle-service.ts:158-176) have no other trigger. The design needs a settle point for BUILD requests, such as a settle on BUILD approval, a team command, or a sync. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts]","action":"Name the entry that settles a BUILD (or other last-stage) request and add a test for it.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"CompletionHook is synchronous with (repo, unit, port) and receives no action; consultHook only calls it for author, build, open-signoff, revise and release.","evidence":"gate.ts:94 `export type CompletionHook = (repo: string, unit: UnitRef, port: TrackerPort) => GateOutcome | 'continue';`. gate.ts:117 HOOKED = ['author','build','open-signoff','revise','release']. gate.ts:123 `registeredHook(repo, unit, port)`. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"teamGate returns allowFirstAuthor before it consults the hook, and allows open-signoff on an unassigned stage.","evidence":"gate.ts:258-262 returns `{ ...ctx.outcome, allowFirstAuthor: true }` when ctx is not ok, before consultHook at line 267. gate.ts:276 `if (holder === null && !CLAIMING.has(action)) return allowed();` where CLAIMING = author, build. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The GitHub adapter's CAPABILITIES lacks signoff-request and its two signoff methods are unsupported; loadTracker rejects a needed capability that is not declared.","evidence":"github-adapter.ts:54 `new Set<Capability>(['claim', 'issue-create'])`. Lines 203-204 return unsupported(...). loadTracker at 215-217 returns rejected with 'does not declare the needed capabilit…'. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.4","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The lifecycle already has open-signoff (approved→in-signoff), signoff-changes and signed-off (in-signoff→…), and complete is legal from approved or signed-off. Editing returns the head to draft.","evidence":"lifecycle.ts:43-46 LIFECYCLE_TABLE entries. lifecycle.ts:250-260 append or move the latest Signoff. The comment at lifecycle.ts:152 says a content change returns the artifact to draft. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Reused helpers exist with the stated shape: approvalStateOf(meta) and lifecycleReviewOf(meta) in approval-view, Lifecycle.signoffs with Signoff{revision, request: Reference, state, actors, at}, and the policy fields signoffStages, claimUnits and source.anchorKnown. SignoffRecord and the signoff module are new.","evidence":"approval-view.ts:30 `export function approvalStateOf(meta: unknown)`, :45 `lifecycleReviewOf(meta: unknown)`. types.ts:131-137 Signoff, :150 `signoffs: readonly Signoff[]`. No existing signoffRecordsOf, settleForAttempt or registerSignoffHook was found in src. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/approval-view.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The request Reference can be stored as { entityId, type: 'signoff-request', relation: 'signoff-of' } with no change to a shared type.","evidence":"types.ts:31 `readonly relation: 'derived-from' | 'depends-on' | 'tracked-by' | 'supersedes' | 'documents' | 'implements' | 'cites' | 'reviews';`, a closed union. 'signoff-of' is not in it, so code written as designed fails strict typecheck. decode.ts:48 accepts any string at runtime, but the type does not. The LLD lists no change site or amendment for Reference, which belongs to the core data model's sc4 lifecycle types. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/decode.ts]","action":"Use an existing relation (e.g. 'tracked-by'), or add 'signoff-of' to the Reference.relation union through an amendment and list types.ts as a change site.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The stage-start entries named for settleForAttempt exist: workflow-step start, runWorkflowServerSide, a second driver entry in workflow-rpc, two build implement entries, and resumeStage.","evidence":"start.ts:61 assertMayAuthor. workflow-rpc.ts:177 runWorkflowServerSide (assertMayAuthor at 183). runStart at 467 has assertMayAuthor at 483. implement.ts:68 and :144 call assertMayBuild. resume.ts:169 `export async function resumeStage`. plan.ts:40, step.ts:38, synthesize.ts:40/70 and validate.ts:222/330/424 are the later phases the design excludes. [files: src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts, src/daemon/steps/build-step/phases/implement.ts, src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/resume.ts, src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/start.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Holding completion at completeThroughService for a held unit also holds the Epic when the Epic is held but the Story is not.","evidence":"gates.ts:945-949 calls `lifecycle.completeIfRolledUp(STORY id…)` once. The walk inside lifecycle-service.ts:161-174 continues to the parent Epic (`next = parent…`) and applies 'complete' to it with no further check. Skipping the call only when the Story is held cannot stop the Epic step. The hold check has to go into the walk, or the walk has to stop at the Story. [files: src/workflow/gates.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts]","action":"Move the signoffHoldsCompletion check into the completion walk per unit, or have completeThroughService pass a predicate that the walk consults for each unit.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Older (grandfathered) artifacts do not block: an artifact approved before the policy anchor is shown as grandfathered and the next stage is not blocked for it.","evidence":"signoffHoldsCompletion (§2.6) is true for any listed LLD/BUILD or DEF/HLD 'not signed off' and does not mention grandfathering. Only signoffRecordsOf applies the anchor. A pre-anchor LLD that stays 'approved' and is never submitted would therefore hold its Story's completion indefinitely. The complete operation (lifecycle.ts:46) is legal from 'approved', so nothing else blocks it. This contradicts the edge-case row for a pre-anchor artifact. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"Have signoffHoldsCompletion and blockedBySignoff apply the same grandfather rule (anchorKnown true and approval before the anchor ⇒ not held), and add a test.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Records with no signoff stay readable, and stored signoffs decode with any Reference shape.","evidence":"decode.ts:39 defaults `signoffs: []`. decode.ts:50-52 isSignoff validates revision, an isReference request (string entityId, type and relation), state and actors, so a stored signoff written by s7 decodes. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/decode.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"sc4 (CompletionHook) and sc1 (SignoffRequestSpec/Ref) are extended only through the named pending amendments AMD-315d510cb28100e2-17 and -16, as additive trailing args or fields.","evidence":"port.ts:45-54 marks SignoffRequestSpec/SignoffRequestRef 'Minimal placeholder; s7 extends it by amendment.' gate.ts:90 says 'Completion hook (declared here, registered by s7)'. The amendment files AMD-315d510cb28100e2-16.json and -17.json exist in .insrc/artifacts (git status). Trailing optional arguments keep a three-argument hook assignable in TS. The Reference.relation addition is not covered by an amendment; it is reported under change-sites. [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each failure case names its detection and response. A partial open-signoff recording is retried idempotently through the stored Reference. A changes-requested request moves only the latest signoff. An illegal open-signoff from completed is detected.","evidence":"lifecycle.ts:257-258 throws IllegalTransitionError unless the latest signoff is open, so signoff-changes and signed-off act on the request that was opened. lifecycle.ts:43 rejects open-signoff from any status other than approved, which matches the 'already completed' terminal case. Gaps found elsewhere: BUILD settle (coverage-of-intent) and the Epic walk (change-sites). [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of ac29–ac35 maps to at least one named unit, contract or integration test, and fixtures reuse existing seams (_setGateDepsForTests, converted-repos helper).","evidence":"The LLD acceptance-mapping table (LLD.md:449-455) lists tests for every ac. gate.ts:87 `_setGateDepsForTests` and src/workflow/__tests__/helpers/converted-repos.js are both used by existing tests (e.g. gate-review-fix.test.ts:34-52). The missing BUILD-request settle path has no test; that follows from the coverage finding. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts, docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/DEF.md]","action":"Add a test for settling a listed BUILD request once that path is designed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":3,"low":11,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-22T15:28:34.467Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
