13978	{"artifactId":"LLD-315d510cb28100e2-s7","entry":{"id":"review-18326160a6dcd54f8d918b9c23145d02","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-22T15:36:04.369Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every s7 acceptance criterion upstream (ac29–ac35) is designed: submit opens one linked request (ac29), refusal names the missing prerequisite (ac30), the next stage is refused while a request is open (ac31), a completed request lets the stage proceed and records all artifacts together (ac32/ac33), unlisted stages are unaffected (ac34), signoff is shown separately (ac35).","evidence":"DEF-315d510cb28100e2.json lines 628-692 list ac29..ac35 with exactly these given/when/then. Each is covered: openSignoff (2.1) for ac29/ac30, blockedBySignoff/settleForAttempt (2.3/2.4) for ac31, settleSignoff (2.2) for ac32/ac33, the no-policy and unlisted-stage invariants for ac34, signoffViewOf plus the ArtifactGate/DeliveryEvidenceEntry/ChainReport fields for ac35. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-315d510cb28100e2.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No non-goal or sibling scope is built: revising an open request (s8) and the tracker-status sync are left out.","evidence":"The adjacent-scope list leaves revision of an open request to s8. The hook only returns 'continue' for revise (2.7) and implements no revise path. The error path for changes-requested says 'The holder revises through s8's flow'.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"CompletionHook is synchronous and receives no action; consultHook calls it only for author, build, open-signoff, revise and release.","evidence":"gate.ts:94 `export type CompletionHook = (repo: string, unit: UnitRef, port: TrackerPort) => GateOutcome | 'continue';`. gate.ts:117 HOOKED = ['author','build','open-signoff','revise','release']. gate.ts:120-126 consultHook calls registeredHook(repo, unit, port). Note: consultHook does not receive `authoring` today (teamGate does), so AMD-17's 'consultHook already holds both' is only half true. Its signature has to gain authoring, and the teamGate call at gate.ts:267 has to pass it. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"When building AMD-17, also change consultHook's signature and its call at gate.ts:267 (outside the cited 94-123 range).","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"teamGate returns allowFirstAuthor before it consults the hook, and returns allowed for a non-claiming action such as open-signoff on an unassigned stage, so openSignoff must check the holder itself.","evidence":"gate.ts:258-262 returns `{...ctx.outcome, allowFirstAuthor: true}` when ctx is not ok, before consultHook at line 267. gate.ts:276 `if (holder === null && !CLAIMING.has(action)) return allowed();` and CLAIMING is only author and build. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"completeIfRolledUp walks upward from the Story to its Epic, so a check made before the call cannot stop the Epic step; its only caller is completeThroughService on a BUILD approval.","evidence":"lifecycle-service.ts:158-176 loops `next = parent`, Story then Epic. A grep for `completeIfRolledUp(` outside tests finds only gates.ts:948 (completeThroughService), and `apply(...'complete'` appears only inside the walk at lifecycle-service.ts:169. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.4","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The GitHub adapter does not declare signoff-request, and SignoffRequestSpec/SignoffRequestRef are minimal placeholders that s7 extends.","evidence":"github-adapter.ts:54 `const CAPABILITIES ... = new Set<Capability>(['claim', 'issue-create']);`. port.ts:45-54 SignoffRequestSpec { title, body } and SignoffRequestRef { ref }, commented 'Minimal placeholder; s7 extends it by amendment.' [files: src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts, src/workflow/tracker/port.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The reused lifecycle facts exist with the stated shape: the Signoff record with a request Reference, the operations open-signoff (from approved), signoff-changes and signed-off (from in-signoff), and 'tracked-by' as a member of the closed relation union.","evidence":"types.ts:31 relation union includes 'tracked-by'. types.ts:131-137 Signoff { revision, request: Reference, state: 'open'|'changes-requested'|'completed', actors, at }. lifecycle.ts:43-46: 'open-signoff' from ['approved'] to in-signoff; signoff-changes and signed-off from ['in-signoff']; complete from ['approved','signed-off']. lifecycle.ts:250-261 appends and moves the latest signoff. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"approvalStateOf, approvedAtOf and lifecycleReviewOf exist and take raw meta, as the design reuses them.","evidence":"approval-view.ts:30, 37 and 45 export all three, each taking `meta: unknown`. approvalStateOf returns only the state (APPROVED_OR_BEYOND includes in-signoff, signed-off and completed). The 'approval at the current revision' check must therefore read lifecycleOfMeta(meta).approval.revision, which is available at approval-view.ts:24. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/approval-view.ts]","action":"Read the approval revision through lifecycleOfMeta, since approvalStateOf does not return it.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The stage-start entries listed for settleForAttempt cover every daemon authoring or build entry: the workflow-step start phase, runWorkflowServerSide, the second driver entry in workflow-rpc, both build implement entries and resumeStage. Later phases are judged by the hook only.","evidence":"assertMayAuthor is called at start.ts:61, workflow-rpc.ts:183 (runWorkflowServerSide entry), workflow-rpc.ts:483 (stream driver entry) and handoff.ts:688 (teamGate author, used by resume). assertMayBuild is called at implement.ts:68 and implement.ts:144. The remaining calls (plan.ts:40, step.ts:38, synthesize.ts:40/70, workflow-rpc.ts:342, validate.ts:222/330/424) are later phases, which the design leaves to the hook. [files: src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/start.ts, src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts, src/daemon/steps/build-step/phases/implement.ts, src/workflow/team/handoff.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The team.settle operation and the teamSettle terminal service fit the existing team.park / team.resume pattern, and hook registration has a place in both processes.","evidence":"handoff-rpc.ts:20-24 returns { 'team.park', 'team.resume' }. cli/services/team.ts:78 teamPark and :89 teamResume take (repoPath, unit, ..., call: DaemonCall). cli/services/index.ts:100-102 makeServices already registers a gate provider (registerParkOfferProvider), and the daemon registers its own in park-offer.ts:30. [files: src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/handoff-rpc.ts, src/cli/services/team.ts, src/cli/services/index.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The unit whose issue a BUILD signoff request is held on, linked from and settled through is defined consistently with the policy's claim units.","evidence":"team/types.ts:37-41 sets `claimUnits: { epic: ['DEF','HLD'], story: ['LLD','PLAN'], task: ['BUILD'] }`, and assertMayBuild (author-gate.ts:52-54) gates a planned build on the task unit. The LLD instead treats BUILD as a Story member: signoffHoldsCompletion says 'a Story whose LLD or BUILD', openSignoff checks 'the Story's code-review record', and settleSignoff reads 'the unit's listed stages'. It never says whether a BUILD request uses the story issue or a task issue for the holder check, the link and settle. Under claimUnits a story unit's listed stages do not include BUILD. [files: src/workflow/team/types.ts, src/workflow/team/author-gate.ts]","action":"State which unit a BUILD submission and its settle use (the story, since the BUILD artifact is story-scoped, or each task), and reconcile it with claimUnits.task = ['BUILD'] in openSignoff's holder check, the request link and settleSignoff's stage selection.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No new stored stamp is needed: signoff facts live in Lifecycle.signoffs, which every converted head carries, and a content change returns the head to draft while keeping earlier signoffs at their revision.","evidence":"types.ts:150 `readonly signoffs: readonly Signoff[]` is a required field of Lifecycle. lifecycle.ts:152-168 reconcileLifecycle returns status 'draft' on a content change and spreads next.lifecycle, keeping the signoffs. The contentHash covers only description, body and citations (lifecycle.ts:102), so meta-only writes such as tracker refs do not reset an in-signoff head. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The grandfathering anchor fields that isSignedOffOrGrandfathered reads exist on TeamPolicy.source.","evidence":"team/types.ts:43-49 source { ref, fetchedAt, firstCommit, firstCommitTime, anchorKnown } and types.ts:22 signoffStages: readonly SignoffStage[] with SignoffStage = 'DEF'|'HLD'|'LLD'|'BUILD'. [files: src/workflow/team/types.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design changes the sc4 hook only additively (AMD-17: trailing action and authoring) and does not redesign the gate, claim or release, which s5 owns.","evidence":"AMD-315d510cb28100e2-17.json declares a sharedContract.fieldAdd on sc4 with `breaking: false` and a signature that appends action and authoring. The LLD keeps teamGate synchronous and rejects the async-gate alternative a2. release() at gate.ts:320 already consults the hook, and the hook returns continue for release. [files: .insrc/artifacts/AMD-315d510cb28100e2-17.json, src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"'A BUILD's request completes but no stage start follows' is detectable because the user sees the BUILD as in-signoff or approved-without-completion in the chain report.","evidence":"chain.ts has no BUILD entry at all. A case-insensitive grep for 'build' in chain.ts matches only the 'Builder' comment and buildChainReport. buildChainReport (chain.ts:86-94) reads only define, hld, stories (readStoryLldStatus), amendments and tracker, and formatChainReport (chain.ts:321+) prints Define/HLD/LLD lines. The new ChainReport signoff field (3.9) adds signoff state 'after the approval state' of existing lines only, so a held BUILD would never be shown there. [files: src/workflow/chain.ts]","action":"Either add a BUILD/Story-completion line to the chain report (and its call site in 3.9), or name a surface that does show a held BUILD (for example the delivery ArtifactGate), so the user knows to run team settle.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion ac29–ac35 maps to at least one named test, and the error paths with the most risk (partial recording, first-author bypass, BUILD code-review check, registration) have tests.","evidence":"The acceptance mapping in §6 lists proving tests for all seven criteria. Unit subjects cover the part-way failure and the Reference round trip (signoff.test.ts), settleForAttempt before allowFirstAuthor (signoff-hook.test.ts), the BUILD CR-record check (signoff.test.ts), registration and entry awaiting (signoff-registration.test.ts) and the completion hold (completion-holds.test.ts, signoff-hold.test.ts). The real-GitHub smoke is marked reported-by-builder.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":2,"low":14,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-22T15:36:04.369Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
