12167	{"artifactId":"LLD-315d510cb28100e2-s7","entry":{"id":"review-704193e880d631613f77ba14d5ddc3ef","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-22T15:44:26.196Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design maps each of the Story's acceptance criteria (ac29-ac35) and does not build ac36 (revision of an open request), which belongs to s8.","evidence":"DEF-315d510cb28100e2.json defines ac29 (submit for signoff), ac30 (refuse when model review or local approval is missing), ac31 (next stage blocked while the request is open), ac32 (completed request then next stage), ac33 (several artifacts complete together), ac34 (unlisted stage), ac35 (signoff shown on records) and ac36 (changes requested, then revise). The LLD's acceptance mapping covers ac29-ac35. For changes-requested the design only records signoff-changes and refuses; the revision itself is left to s8. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-315d510cb28100e2.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"CompletionHook is synchronous and takes no action argument; consultHook calls it only for author, build, open-signoff, revise and release.","evidence":"gate.ts:94 `export type CompletionHook = (repo: string, unit: UnitRef, port: TrackerPort) => GateOutcome | 'continue';`. gate.ts:117 `HOOKED = new Set(['author','build','open-signoff','revise','release'])`. gate.ts:123 `return registeredHook(repo, unit, port);`. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"teamGate returns allowFirstAuthor before it consults the hook, and returns allowed with no holder check for open-signoff on an unassigned stage. So the entry-level settleForAttempt check and openSignoff's own holder read are both needed.","evidence":"gate.ts:258-263: a no-issue first author turn returns `{ ...ctx.outcome, allowFirstAuthor: true }` before consultHook runs at line 267. gate.ts:276: `if (holder === null && !CLAIMING.has(action)) return allowed();` where CLAIMING holds only author and build. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"completeIfRolledUp walks upward from a unit to its parent, completing each unit whose roll-up holds. EvidenceContext carries only overrideReview, so a check made before the call cannot stop the Epic step.","evidence":"lifecycle-service.ts:27-29: EvidenceContext is `{ overrideReview? }`. Lines 158-176: a while loop runs rollUp, then apply 'complete', then `next = parentOf(key)`. gates.ts:945-949: completeThroughService calls completeIfRolledUp on the STORY after a BUILD approval. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.4","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The GitHub adapter does not support openSignoffRequest or readSignoffState, and its CAPABILITIES lack signoff-request. loadTracker rejects a needed capability that the adapter does not declare.","evidence":"github-adapter.ts:54 `CAPABILITIES = new Set(['claim', 'issue-create'])`. Lines 203-204 return `unsupported(...)`. Lines 215-217: loadTracker returns rejected when missingCapabilities finds a gap. port.ts:20 already lists 'signoff-request' in the Capability union. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts, src/workflow/tracker/port.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The reused lifecycle machinery has the stated shape. Lifecycle.signoffs exists. open-signoff runs only from approved and needs a request Reference. signed-off and signoff-changes move the latest open Signoff. complete is legal from signed-off. Reference.relation is a closed union that includes 'tracked-by', so no type change is needed.","evidence":"types.ts:31 relation union includes 'tracked-by'. types.ts:131-137 Signoff is { revision, request: Reference, state, actors, at }. types.ts:150 `signoffs: readonly Signoff[]`. lifecycle.ts:43-46: open-signoff from ['approved'] to in-signoff; signed-off from ['in-signoff']; complete from ['approved','signed-off']. lifecycle.ts:250-260: open-signoff calls needReference(detail.request), and signed-off moves the latest open signoff. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"approvalStateOf, approvedAtOf and lifecycleReviewOf exist and take raw meta, as isSignedOffOrGrandfathered, openSignoff and signoffViewOf assume. Approval stays 'approved' through in-signoff, changes-requested and signed-off.","evidence":"approval-view.ts:18 APPROVED_OR_BEYOND = ['approved','in-signoff','changes-requested','signed-off','completed']. Line 30 approvalStateOf(meta). Line 37 approvedAtOf(meta). Line 45 lifecycleReviewOf(meta). [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/approval-view.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.3","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"TeamPolicy exposes signoffStages, source.firstCommitTime and source.anchorKnown. claimUnits puts BUILD on task units, which motivates the rule that a request belongs to the Story's issue.","evidence":"team/types.ts:22 `signoffStages: readonly SignoffStage[]`. Lines 37-41: claimUnits.task is ['BUILD']. Lines 43-49: source has firstCommitTime and anchorKnown. [files: src/workflow/team/types.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The listed stage-start entries cover every daemon place where a next stage begins: the workflow-step start phase, runWorkflowServerSide, the second driver entry in workflow-rpc, the two build implement entries and resumeStage. The later phases call the gate only, which reaches the hook.","evidence":"Entry gates in the code: start.ts:61 assertMayAuthor; workflow-rpc.ts:183 (runWorkflowServerSide); workflow-rpc.ts:483 (runStart, the driver entry); implement.ts:68 and :144 assertMayBuild; handoff.ts:688 teamGate in resume. The pre-write recheck at workflow-rpc.ts:342, plan.ts:40, step.ts:38, synthesize.ts:40/70 and the validate.ts entries are later phases, as the design states. [files: src/daemon/workflow-rpc.ts, src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/phases/start.ts, src/daemon/steps/build-step/phases/implement.ts, src/workflow/team/handoff.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The hook needs the action and the authoring workflow. AMD-315d510cb28100e2-17 adds them as additive trailing arguments, and consultHook already has both values.","evidence":"AMD-17 sets the type to `(repo, unit, port, action: GuardedAction, authoring?: string) => GateOutcome | 'continue'`. In gate.ts:254 teamGate receives `authoring`, and at line 120 consultHook receives `action`; adding the arguments is a threading-only change. authorUnitOf (author-gate.ts:24-34) gives a story unit for design.story and plan, so followedStageOf has to derive the epic for HLD, as designed. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts, src/workflow/team/author-gate.ts, .insrc/artifacts/AMD-315d510cb28100e2-17.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"team.settle can be added beside team.park and team.resume in handoffRpcHandlers.","evidence":"handoff-rpc.ts:20-25 returns an RpcHandlers map with 'team.park' and 'team.resume'. A third key fits that pattern. [files: src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/handoff-rpc.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No new stored stamp is added. Signoff facts use the existing Lifecycle.signoffs field, and a head with no signoffs reads as state 'none'. SignoffRequestSpec and SignoffRequestRef are placeholders that are extended additively by AMD-16.","evidence":"port.ts:45-54: SignoffRequestSpec { title, body } and SignoffRequestRef { ref } are marked 'Minimal placeholder; s7 extends it by amendment'. AMD-16 adds `{ unit; artifacts: {artifactId, revision, path}[]; branch; issue }`. Lifecycle.signoffs is already required in the model (types.ts:150). [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/types.ts, .insrc/artifacts/AMD-315d510cb28100e2-16.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design changes the sc4 hook signature only through the filed amendment and does not redesign the gate (s5) or the port (s1). The delivery types it extends with a signoff entry are additive fields.","evidence":"CompletionHook (gate.ts:94) is changed only through AMD-17, and the adapter request types only through AMD-16. ArtifactGate (delivery/types.ts:188-203) and DeliveryEvidenceEntry (280-290) gain an optional-style signoff entry while approval and review keep their values. registerCompletionHook (gate.ts:100) has no caller yet, consistent with s5 shipping it unregistered. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts, src/workflow/delivery/types.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A completed artifact cannot be submitted for signoff: open-signoff is illegal from completed. A completion walk without a hold would complete a held Story's approved LLD or BUILD through the cascade. The holds predicate is therefore what keeps listed members submittable.","evidence":"lifecycle.ts:43 open-signoff runs only from ['approved']. lifecycle-service.ts:248-258: completeMember cascades complete onto any non-terminal member. lifecycle.ts:349-362: a Story's members include LLD and BUILD; an Epic's include DEF and HLD. This matches the design's terminal error case and its invariant. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle-service.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion ac29-ac35 maps to at least one named test, and the existing test fixtures the strategy relies on exist.","evidence":"The acceptance-mapping table lists proving tests for ac29 through ac35. gate.ts:87 exports the `_setGateDepsForTests` seam named as a fixture, with readPolicy, loadTracker, resolveIssue, ensureIssue and artifactExists. The GitHub smoke test is declared as reported by the builder. [files: src/workflow/team/gate.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":15,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-22T15:44:26.196Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
